    "K_t": "Evidence:\n[1] The Pepsi-Cola Made with Real Sugar, formerly called Throwback, is a brand of soft drink sold by PepsiCo in the United States and in sweet stores in South Australia for its flagship Pepsi and Mountain Dew brands.\n[2] Pepsi is a carbonated soft drink produced and manufactured by PepsiCo.\n[3] It is the market leader of lemon soft drinks in Australia and grew by over 30% in 2007.\n[4] The drinks, called Pepsi Throwback and Mountain Dew Throwback, are named as such because they are flavored with cane sugar and beet sugar instead of high fructose corn syrup, which soft drink companies used to replace sugar (in their North American products) in the 1980s."
